cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this methods package, please cite it as below."
title: "The Jury Methods Package: Synthetic Survey Respondents on Pew ATP Wave 158"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-21"
url: "https://corman.io/writing/the-jury/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zzirblake/the-jury-public"
authors:
  - family-names: "Corman"
    given-names: "Blake"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7656-0695"
abstract: "A public-safe methods package for a 1,000-juror synthetic respondent panel benchmarked against Pew American Trends Panel Wave 158. The artifact shows that probability-vector polling substantially mitigates within-cell variance compression on 10 of 11 questions while overall validation still fails through topic-specific marginal error."
keywords:
  - synthetic respondents
  - survey methodology
  - large language models
  - public opinion
  - probability-vector polling
  - distributional alignment
